| \\\\  & =|0-35| \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84701/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84701"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12281/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer/id #uuid "79aedc25-2c35-5c52-9bd6-19c2f259f297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12281/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "cb455426-2ecb-5722-a4aa-896d921ccf55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12281/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" :answer/id #uuid "4b431516-82ff-59d8-9299-5b6d857660b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12281/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "7d0969fa-9091-5f54-83fd-eef98a6207fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12281/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "f0f90746-b6f5-594b-b1ae-e8354e27cd34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12281/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc4bc45-5ebd-52f0-a4b8-7401155ede6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12281/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer-field/choices ["q-12281/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" "q-12281/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-12281/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" "q-12281/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-12281/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12281" :question/id #uuid "e681021f-00b8-50ac-8a56-4466dbb53174" :question/math-academy-id "q-12281" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/d9e210f0bfd9ada2dd147068fe0cf06fa85ad049f79bb7e844931b6037867f97.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=2\\cdot 4=8.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=5\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 3=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-12281/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12281"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-9302"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/4f31b9f180b1b766451685428fc289766832fe5d0c7d8902a601ebf060eab0e7.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 0=-10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-10|\\cdot 4\\pi  \\\\  & =40\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-9311/selection/4a03be6ca5a931097242157323e96fac707848be6f9e14b789a4470740e06647" :answer/id #uuid "f8e4825e-4664-559b-ac26-bd9b920fa6db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "121" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9311/selection/16943fbe431b8ad65062bb7a8cd5d2f82696bba5ae52194b653416a034b2e8e1" :answer/id #uuid "25b69aad-6d9b-51d4-bcad-3a61d0dafdd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "152" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9311/selection/a3895aead52b4194a0c7cbddd283c827ff3805cbe2457302fcb1ba6942b721a8" :answer/id #uuid "183681bc-d490-50df-9982-d5abef86ec97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-152" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9311/selection/95ac9798bd3315a98d8f0f9c222cebe407c91ed3a370285640c99e069d3b8743" :answer/id #uuid "2145e9cd-9159-5c45-9da3-dc2b06db3c1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "320" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9311/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "b7c07e3d-af06-5b8e-9884-4fc0d5856c49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9311/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "732b52ff-670f-5504-a3fa-41c8362516b8" :answer-field/ke