re,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316588/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316588"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316591/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "41c466f5-12a2-5326-8360-dbac1c75312e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316591/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2dd50da-f51e-570d-a033-74dc33383755" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316591/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-316591/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316591" :question/id #uuid "bca98248-d03b-5f6b-b96d-7295f22821a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316591" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/455e0a08e2a0929a60d7fa1b76973e1b7a460efe8cc1cf01719ce211feacd8c0.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-5\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316591/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85073/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "706f557a-719f-52f6-9e63-2d3f4b2d9d8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85073/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer/id #uuid "55e29dc6-9969-527f-814b-5543bd045230" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85073/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" :answer/id #uuid "5b50e6e2-80aa-5a06-9b77-0391e59a6f60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85073/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "7ef67f89-9929-56ca-b481-9b7c306ac8c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85073/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "71726a20-fe1d-5adc-bdeb-0b79ddcd9258" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85073/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1342dba8-ec03-5d36-b4d2-b053ea848428" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85073/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-85073/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" "q-85073/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" "q-85073/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" "q-85073/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-85073/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85073" :question/id #uuid "560a0a6d-8e26-5a12-badb-d4317fbbe50b" :question/math-academy-id "q-85073" :question/problem "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(-2,-1),(3,-1),(1,3).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/10c831c616279f443d10ed478a8b3b173d598da6e9b0b45edb7ecf487cf97f92.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 4=10.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,6\\,|\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-85073/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85073"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275981/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "f46ad528-cc2b-522d-a59e-d2d1226b8d21" :answer/type :answ