n.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275981/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275981"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316612/field-1/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "7420781d-c155-5ad9-85a4-980929bb46b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316612/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac4dd13f-f7d6-5ce7-ba52-dcc407db93d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316612/field-1/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer-field/choices ["q-316612/field-1/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316612" :question/id #uuid "b465aaa4-ff86-5876-9f66-66b7eb23fbbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-316612" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,1),(6,1),(5,4).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/92ee29a22baa10f4af25db8221e7d67c729f5f0f1b5e1b3c37aee7e31a92bdfb.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-3)=4+3=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,7\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316612/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316606/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "067bb28f-70ae-5ca2-916c-78f24134099e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316606/field-1/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" :answer/id #uuid "46e7464d-7629-5806-aa07-04e5640e39cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316606/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c99caa6-f201-5a73-979b-5074f5344bf3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316606/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer-field/choices ["q-316606/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-316606/field-1/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316606" :question/id #uuid "d412caa5-3690-592c-8eec-aa466eedc1b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316606" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1),(5,1),(3,4).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/3e2c56766f201095bee0eea101b877e30910c676c998f37d261fd7cf7aabb837.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-6\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316606/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316606"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316607/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "758a80e2-fef0-5d0c-9131-acf560683f72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316607/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a06e39e-da10-5b2b-801f-8c68b17f7337" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316607/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-316607/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316607" :question/id #uuid "423d63ac-43bc-545e-9007-0b2aae970538" :question/math-academy-id "q-316607" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(0,0),(6,0),(2,5).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/059560835586e9c149cdb5dabcddc80610a58bfa0c30cb5f685b8bb6bdca3e90.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 5=15.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316607/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7454"] :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|\\det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|8-3| \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5470"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/e8ff769df4089e6ed9a47d56d7317acf41b8aef6a255abc705c0e7ec31a446ea.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 -  2 \\cdot (-1) = 10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5471"] :question/problem "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5),$ and $(-2,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/ee8f0cf16983d87fa505303ed6372a3f389518d05b3e13f2e9e2121038792b84.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 -  5 \\cdot (-2) = -11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-11|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
